From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] flow: CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS clocks named hard blocks later or
 earlier

A parent over hardened blocks can want each block's clock somewhere
other than where CTS's latency balance puts it: block-granular useful
skew on its crossings, or a block whose clock route speeds up more than
the register tree's between CTS's placement parasitics and global route,
made up for at CTS. On XiangShan's XSTile the blocks were balanced within
-31..+23 ps at CTS and arrived -98..+22 ps at global route; the best
block-granular offsets measured there are tens of ps either way.

CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS is <instance> <offset> pairs, the offset in the
platform's time unit; before clock_tree_synthesis each named instance,
which must be a hard block, gets cts::set_latency_offset (carried
OpenROAD patch 0240), and the latency balancer clocks it that much later
than balanced, earlier for a negative offset. Empty, the default,
changes nothing. On an OpenROAD without cts::set_latency_offset the
stage stops on the unknown command rather than building an unskewed
tree.

Not upstreamed; retires at a bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 docs/user/FlowVariables.md  |  2 ++
 flow/scripts/cts.tcl        | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 flow/scripts/variables.yaml |  8 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/user/FlowVariables.md b/docs/user/FlowVariables.md
index 1455aa1..9be7aa1 100644
--- a/docs/user/FlowVariables.md
+++ b/docs/user/FlowVariables.md
@@ -131,6 +131,7 @@ configuration file.
 | <a name="CTS_BUF_LIST"></a>CTS_BUF_LIST| List of cells used to construct the clock tree. Overrides buffer inference.| |
 | <a name="CTS_CLUSTER_DIAMETER"></a>CTS_CLUSTER_DIAMETER| Maximum diameter (in microns) of sink cluster.| |
 | <a name="CTS_CLUSTER_SIZE"></a>CTS_CLUSTER_SIZE| Maximum number of sinks per cluster.| |
+| <a name="CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS"></a>CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS| Pairs of a hard block instance and an offset in the platform's time unit: CTS's latency balancer clocks the block that much later than balanced, earlier for a negative offset. Block-granular useful skew, or a parasitic drift between CTS and global route made up for.| |
 | <a name="CTS_LIB_NAME"></a>CTS_LIB_NAME| Name of the Liberty library to use in selecting the clock buffers.| |
 | <a name="CTS_USEFUL_SKEW"></a>CTS_USEFUL_SKEW| Enable useful skew during the CTS balancing phase.| 0|
 | <a name="DESIGN_NAME"></a>DESIGN_NAME| The name of the top-level module of the design.| |
@@ -558,6 +559,7 @@ configuration file.
 - [CTS_BUF_LIST](#CTS_BUF_LIST)
 - [CTS_CLUSTER_DIAMETER](#CTS_CLUSTER_DIAMETER)
 - [CTS_CLUSTER_SIZE](#CTS_CLUSTER_SIZE)
+- [CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS](#CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS)
 - [CTS_LIB_NAME](#CTS_LIB_NAME)
 - [CTS_USEFUL_SKEW](#CTS_USEFUL_SKEW)
 - [DETAILED_METRICS](#DETAILED_METRICS)
diff --git a/flow/scripts/cts.tcl b/flow/scripts/cts.tcl
index ca0c9aa..5a4dbbe 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/cts.tcl
+++ b/flow/scripts/cts.tcl
@@ -27,6 +27,22 @@ if { [env_var_exists_and_non_empty CTS_ARGS] } {
 
 set_dont_use $::env(DONT_USE_CELLS)
 
+# Block-granular clock skew the flow chooses: each named hard block's clock
+# lands that much later than CTS's latency balance (negative: earlier).
+if { [env_var_exists_and_non_empty CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS] } {
+  set offsets $::env(CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS)
+  if { [llength $offsets] % 2 != 0 } {
+    utl::error FLW 50 "CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS is <instance> <offset> pairs: $offsets"
+  }
+  foreach {name offset} $offsets {
+    set inst [[ord::get_db_block] findInst $name]
+    if { $inst == "NULL" || ![[$inst getMaster] isBlock] } {
+      utl::error FLW 50 "CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS: $name is not a hard block instance."
+    }
+    log_cmd cts::set_latency_offset $name $offset
+  }
+}
+
 log_cmd clock_tree_synthesis {*}$cts_args
 
 if { $::env(DETAILED_METRICS) } {
diff --git a/flow/scripts/variables.yaml b/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
index c482a73..9c9daf9 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
+++ b/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
@@ -1379,6 +1379,14 @@ CTS_CLUSTER_SIZE:
     - cts
   tunable: 1
   type: int
+CTS_LATENCY_OFFSETS:
+  description: |
+    Pairs of a hard block instance and an offset in the platform's time
+    unit: CTS's latency balancer clocks the block that much later than
+    balanced, earlier for a negative offset. Block-granular useful skew,
+    or a parasitic drift between CTS and global route made up for.
+  stages:
+    - cts
 CTS_LIB_NAME:
   description: |
     Name of the Liberty library to use in selecting the clock buffers.
